# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD is `/usr/local/sbin/hs-start.sh`, which backgrounds sshd,
# php-fpm8.2 (pool running as root, world-writable socket), nginx (path-info
# RCE vhost + private catch-all + autoindex), cron and the planted ncat
# listener, then `wait`s. So every seeded misconfiguration is LIVE at first
# boot, which is what makes verify.sh's behavioural probes (HTTP RCE via
# webshell, pathinfo exec, posix_getuid pool probe, autoindex/server_tokens
# headers, private-vhost Host: leak, nc :$listener_port) meaningful.
#
# PID 1 is hs-start.sh (a `wait` over all daemons), NOT any single service,
# so a solution may restart php-fpm and reload nginx without killing the
# container.
#
# Without this marker the harness overrides CMD with `sleep infinity`: no
# daemon boots, every service check fails (-10 each) and the service-dependent
# non-service checks become meaningless (false-pass).
